cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Brink, please cite it as below."
title: "Brink: detecting and preventing LLM safety collapse during fine-tuning"
abstract: >-
  Brink stops fine-tuning from breaking a language model's safety. It scores training samples and drops
  those that would erode the model's refusals, monitors a refusal signal on probe prompts during training with
  an alarm calibrated on safe fine-tuning only, and on the alarm rolls the model back to its last safe state
  and continues with a gradient guard that blocks further erosion. Built on Cohere's Tiny Aya and the Lexsi
  Labs open-source toolkits.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/andrew1234-arch/brink"
authors:
  - name: Cmg
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - alignment
  - fine-tuning
  - refusal direction
  - safety drift
